# The repository root's ignore file, and the belt to the braces of the four that
# Flutter put inside `src/`. Those four already cover the per-platform build
# leavings; this one exists for everything *above* `src/`, which nothing else
# ignores at all — a `.DS_Store` dropped beside the Makefile, or a signing key
# parked at the root on the way to a release, would otherwise be swept up by the
# first `git add -A`. Rules that duplicate `src/.gitignore` are kept anyway:
# they cost nothing and they hold if that file is ever regenerated by Flutter.
#
# Laid out to match `../rollhippo/.gitignore`, deliberately, like the rest of
# this repository.

# ── Build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
build/
src/build/
src/.dart_tool/
src/.flutter-plugins
src/.flutter-plugins-dependencies
src/.packages
*.iml

# ── Credentials — never commit any of these ───────────────────────────────────
# Prophylactic. None of these paths exist yet and most of the tooling that would
# make them — fastlane, a release env — has not arrived. That is the point: the
# rule has to be in place before the file is, because the one time it matters is
# the time nobody was looking.
release.env
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p8
*.p12
*.pem
*.cer
*.mobileprovision
*.provisionprofile
src/android/key.properties
src/ios/ExportOptions.plist
fastlane/*.json
!fastlane/Appfile
.keys/
certs/
keys/

# ── Generated, and tracked anyway — do not add these ──────────────────────────
# `make icon`, `make boop` and `make audio` write into the project rather than
# into /tmp, and the files they write are tracked on purpose: the icon rasters
# in the three platform catalogues *are* the icon, `assets/boop.wav` *is* the
# sound, and the four `assets/audio/*.ogg` *are* the soundtrack. A clone has to
# build and run without ffmpeg installed and without anyone running a tool
# first. Anyone tidying generated output out of version control should stop
# here: these are output the way a compiled-in constant is output.
#
# What is genuinely disposable goes to /tmp/mazehippo instead — `make board`
# renders there and `make clean` removes it — so it never reaches this file.

# ── iOS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
src/ios/Pods/
src/ios/.symlinks/
src/ios/Flutter/Flutter.framework
src/ios/Flutter/Flutter.podspec
src/ios/Flutter/Generated.xcconfig
src/ios/Flutter/flutter_export_environment.sh
src/ios/Runner/GeneratedPluginRegistrant.*
**/xcuserdata/
**/DerivedData/

# ── Android ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
src/android/.gradle/
src/android/local.properties
src/android/app/debug/
src/android/app/profile/
src/android/app/release/
src/android/gradle-wrapper.jar.sha256

# ── Tooling ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.dart_tool/
.pub-cache/
.pub/
coverage/
*.log

# ── macOS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
